\label{def:query-system}



A \emph{query system} is a preordered family of queries with coherent refinement maps. It consists of:
\begin{itemize}
\item An index type $\iota$
\item A family of queries $q : \iota \to \text{Query}$
\item A preorder relation $\le$ on indices
\item Refinement maps $\pi : \forall \{i\ j\}, i \le j \to \text{Refine}(q_i, q_j)$
\end{itemize}
subject to functoriality conditions.

\label{def:cylinder}


A \emph{cylinder set} $\text{Cyl}(i, A)$ is the set of realizations where query $i$ yields an outcome in $A$.
These generate the observable $\sigma$-algebra.

\label{def:compatible-marginals}



A family $\nu$ of measures on query outcomes is \emph{compatible} if the measures commute with refinement maps:
whenever $i \le j$, the pushforward of $\nu_i$ along $\pi_{ij}$ equals $\nu_j$.

\label{def:upper-directed}


A query system is \emph{upper-directed} if any two queries have a common
refinement: $\forall i\,j, \exists k, i \le k \land j \le k$.

\label{def:stone-clopens}



The sets $\{u : E \in u\}$ for $E$ a cylinder event. These are clopen, form a
set semiring, and generate the $\sigma$-algebra used on $\mathrm{St}(S)$.

\label{def:ncc}


A family $\nu_i$ of finitely additive contents on the outcome spaces,
compatible under refinement, each of total mass $1$. Finitely additive only.

\label{lem:ce-levelwise}



$\nu$ is collectively exhaustive if and only if every $\nu_i$ is continuous at
$\emptyset$, i.e. $\sigma$-additive.

\label{thm:sp1-iff}



Collective exhaustion holds if and only if every level's content extends to a
genuine measure on that level's outcome space.

\label{lem:cylgen-sigma-subadd}



Under sequential upper-directedness (with surjective evaluations and
compatible marginal measures) the cylinder content is $\sigma$-subadditive.

\label{def:escaping-tower}



  A decreasing sequence of cylinder events, each of full charge, with empty
intersection.

\label{def:aj-A}


$A = \mathbb{Z} + \alpha\mathbb{Z}$ for $\alpha$ irrational (as a set, and as
the additive subgroup \texttt{Afull} of $\mathbb{R}$). Countable.

\label{lem:aj-V}



  $V$, a set of coset representatives for $\mathbb{R}/A$: two representatives
congruent mod $A$ are equal.

\label{thm:aj-finite}



For FINITE $F \subseteq A$, the set $V + F$ contains no measurable set of
positive measure.

\label{thm:trace-measure}



For $X$ thick for $\mu$, the traces $\{E \cap X\}$ carry a measure with
$\lambda_X(E \cap X) = \mu(E)$ (Border, Prop.~14).

\label{thm:aj-hypotheses}



The Andersen--Jessen system is upper-directed, and every level's evaluation is
onto.

\label{lem:diag-inter}



$\bigcap_n D_n = \{\omega : \omega_i = \omega_0 \text{ for all } i\}$: the
sequences that are constant outright.

\label{thm:diag-empty}



  If $\bigcap_k Y_k = \emptyset$ then $\Pi'(Y) \cap \bigcap_n D_n = \emptyset$,
generically in $Y$.

\label{lem:cont-above}


A probability measure cannot give every term of an antitone measurable sequence
mass one when the intersection is empty.

\label{thm:delay-qs}



$(d,\tau) \mapsto$ the delay query, with the refinement above, satisfies the
query-system axioms.

Reflexivity and transitivity of the order are divisibility and arithmetic;
$\pi_{\mathrm{refl}}$ and $\pi_{\mathrm{trans}}$ are index computations on
coordinate selections.

\label{def:delay-fixed-lag}



Fix a lag $\tau_0$ and a maximum depth $N$; index by $\{d \leq N\}$ with the
order $d \leq d'$ and coordinate-truncation refinement.

\label{def:observable-algebra}



The $\sigma$-algebra on the state space generated by a family
$f : \mathbb{Z} \to (X \to \mathbb{R})$;
$\mathcal{O}_h := \mathrm{observableAlgebra}(n \mapsto h \circ T^{n})$
(\texttt{delayObservableAlgebra}).

\label{thm:delay-eval-iterate}



$\mathrm{delayEval}\,d\,\tau\,(\mathrm{orbitStream}\,h\,T\,x)
 = (\Phi_h^{T^{\tau}}(x)_k)_{k<d}$.

\label{lem:val-inter}



On an intersection-closed carrier a two-valued state is \emph{multiplicative}:
if $A$ and $A'$ are true, so is $A \cap A'$.

\label{def:mo2}



The six-element lattice $\{\bot, a, a', b, b', \top\}$ with the four middle
elements pairwise incomparable, $a^{\perp} = a'$ and $b^{\perp} = b'$.

\label{thm:concrete-mo2-meets}



Any two members of $L$ have a greatest member of $L$ below both. In
particular $A \wedge B = \emptyset$ while $A \cap B \neq \emptyset$.

\label{def:l2n}



$L_2^N := \mathrm{Fin}\,N \to \mathrm{MO}_2$, carrying the product lattice
order: $x \le y$ iff $x_i \le y_i$ at every block $i$.

\label{thm:star-finite}



For every $N$ and every block $i < N$,
\[ p \sqcap a_i = \bot \quad\text{and}\quad p \not\le a_i^{\perp}. \]

\label{thm:star-infinite}



For Navara's witness $p$ and every $n$ in the countable orthogonal family,
\[ p \sqcap a_n = \bot \quad\text{and}\quad p \not\le a_n^{\perp}. \]

\label{thm:prod-oml}



If each $\alpha_i$ is an orthomodular lattice then so is $\prod_i \alpha_i$,
with lattice operations, bounds and orthocomplement all coordinatewise.

\label{lem:afam-ortho}



For $n \ne m$, $a_n \le a_m^{\perp}$. The family is indexed by $\mathbb{N}$,
so it is infinite.

\label{thm:boolean-baseline}



On an intersection-closed carrier every finitely coherent local pattern has
nonempty kernel: some Dirac state extends it.

\label{def:finadd-state}



Pair additivity only. Finite-family additivity is derived
(\texttt{val\_sUnion\_finset}).

\label{lem:pattern-fully-additive}



A finitely coherent \texttt{LocalState} satisfies every Def-1.2 constraint on
$B$.

\label{lem:coreblock-disjoint}



On the witness's own block the only disjoint pairs are the complement pairs, so
there \texttt{LocalState} equals Def 1.2-on-$B$ exactly, coherence or not.

\label{lem:boolean-no-witness}



On an intersection-closed (Boolean) carrier no $\sigma$-essential contextual
state exists (Prop 2.1).

\label{def:core-block}



$\Omega = \omega_1 \times \{1,2,3,4\}$ with cores $A_1 = M\times\{1,2\}$,
$A_2 = M\times\{1,3\}$, $A_3 = M\times\{2,3\}$; $L$ the least $\sigma$-class
containing singletons, cells and cores; $B$ the $\perp$-closure of the cores;
$s_0 \equiv 1$ on the three cores, encoded as the majority vote of three marked
points (self-dual, so the complement values are forced).

\label{thm:psi-zfc}



$\Psi$ holds on $\sigma$-classes/OMPs, irreducible modulo the countable ideal,
in ZFC.

\label{thm:normal-form}



Every set in the carrier has a normalized representation, with coordinate $3$ as
the anchor.

\label{thm:vote-state}



The majority-vote assignment is a finitely additive two-valued state on the
whole carrier, and it extends the core pattern.

\label{lem:finite-sigma}



On a finite $\Omega$ every finitely additive state satisfies the
$\sigma$-condition on the whole carrier.

\label{thm:one-block-iff-boolean}



A carrier has a unique maximal block if and only if it is intersection-closed.
Hence $\Phi$ holds on one-block carriers.

\label{lem:concentration-partition}



If the carrier contains a countable partition of $\Omega$, every
$\sigma$-additive two-valued state is true on exactly one part.

\label{lem:witness-not-lattice}



$L_1$ has no meet at the cores: a greatest lower bound would have to be the
slab $M \times \{0\}$, which is not in the carrier.

\label{cor:carrier-not-orderiso}



There is no order isomorphism between the carrier of $L_1$ and the measurable
sets of a $\sigma$-algebra, on any space.

\label{def:central}



$E$ lies in the carrier and $E \cap A$ is again in the carrier for every carrier
element $A$.

\label{thm:central-traces}



A central $E$ has a single $\xi$ with $\mathrm{trace}(E,f) \approx \xi$ for every
coordinate $f$.

\label{def:segregated}



A carrier is \emph{segregated} when every finitely additive state is blockwise
pointed --- each maximal block supplies a kernel point. \emph{Non-segregated}
is the negation.



Essential irreducibility is \ref{cor:centre}: every central element of $L_1$ is
countable or co-countable. Non-segregation is \ref{lem:witness-nonsegregated}
applied to the witness of \ref{thm:psi-zfc}.

\label{def:irreducible}



The centre is trivial: every central element is $\emptyset$ or $\Omega$.
Strictly stronger than \ref{def:essentially-irreducible}.

\label{def:psi-oml}



The same existence sentence with latticehood (\texttt{MeetsExist}) adjoined to
the carrier.

\label{def:countably-compact-class}


A family $\mathcal{K}$ of sets such that every sequence from $\mathcal{K}$
with the finite intersection property has nonempty total intersection.

\label{def:inner-regular-81}



Every value-$1$ member of the field contains a value-$1$ in-field
\emph{compact}.

\label{def:cocountable-state}



On an uncountable $\Omega$, the countable/co-countable $\sigma$-field with the
state that is $1$ exactly on the co-countable sets.

\label{lem:cocountable-not-dirac}



For every $\omega$ there is a carrier set of value $1$ missing $\omega$ ---
namely $\{\omega\}^{c}$.

\label{thm:cocountable-fails-81}



On an uncountable second-countable Hausdorff space, (8.1) fails at the
specific set $F = X \setminus \{x\}$ for $x$ a condensation point.

\label{cor:cocountable-fails-hausdorff}



On \emph{any} uncountable Hausdorff space the co-countable state fails (8.1)
somewhere --- no second countability needed.

\label{lem:conjugation}



If $r$ is a unit of $\mathbb{Z}_k$, that is $\gcd(r,k)=1$, then
$\mathrm{TR}_k^{(r)}(L)$ holds iff $\mathrm{TR}_k^{(1)}(L)$ does.

\label{thm:pruning}



For every $\rho$, every $L \geq 1$, every $k \geq 1$ and every $r$ generating
$\mathbb{Z}_k$, $\mathrm{LISC}_k(L)$ holds iff $\mathrm{TR}_k^{(r)}(L)$ does.

\label{lem:unsafe-biunion}



For finite $A$, $\mathrm{Unsafe}(\rho)$ is the union of $\mathrm{TR}_k^{(1)}$
over $2 \leq k \leq |A|$.

\label{lem:iterate}


For $f : \beta \to \beta$ with $\beta$ finite and any $b$, there are $s$ and
$p > 0$ with $f^{n+p}(b) = f^{n}(b)$ for all $n \geq s$.

\label{lem:evper-tr}



For finite $A$, the set of $L$ with $\mathrm{TR}_k^{(1)}(L)$ is eventually
periodic.

\label{def:cycle-stream}



From a cycle witness $W$ and modulus $n$, the stream carrying $W$ at index
$(-t) \bmod n$. It is $n$-periodic (\texttt{cycleStream\_periodic}).

\label{thm:lisc-delay-witness}



If $\mathrm{LISC}_k(L)$ then there is a $\rho$-trajectory $\omega$, periodic
of period $kL$, whose depth-$k$, lag-$L$ delay query is injective.

\label{cor:unsafe-delay}



$L \in \mathrm{Unsafe}(\rho)$ yields a periodic $\rho$-trajectory on which
the lag-$L$ delay query resolves $k \geq 2$ distinct strands.

\label{lem:lisc-inhabited}



The complete relation on $\{\bot,\top\}$ satisfies $\mathrm{LISC}_2(1)$, so
the conclusion of \ref{thm:lisc-delay-witness} is inhabited.

\label{lem:delay-nonpos}



Streams agreeing at every $t \leq 0$ are indistinguishable to every delay
query.
